# AI working state

Globally-useful state only. Detail lives in `state/<track>.md` — see the
index below. Read this file first every session; read a track's state file
only when you are touching that track.

## Latest

Channels. A channel is a fan-out (one Ring per codec), a rate limit and a
member list; connections hold many memberships, each with its own write
pump. `JOIN`/`PART`/`NAMES` with presence, per-channel backlog and rate
limits, channels created on demand and reclaimed when empty. The
`Channels` hook decides where a connection starts (`Autojoin`) and where
it may go (`CanJoin`). Detail in `state/server.md`; the fan-out
underneath is in `state/broadcast.md`.

Two defects were found and fixed on the way: the config defaults for
`Capacity` and `DebugAddr` had never actually been applied despite two
commits claiming so, because the test that was supposed to catch drift
compared an all-commented file against the code — that is, `Default()`
against itself. The test now uncomments the file and checks the
documented values really are the defaults, and that every field is
documented.

## State file index

- `state/broadcast.md` — `internal/broadcast`, the fan-out primitive and
  its comparative benchmark harness.
- `state/server.md` — config, wire codecs, extension points, and the
  connection handling built on the fan-out.

